  clock: 8  # e8c2
  nonce: e8c2  # e8c2
  message: "ADR-0057 §10-§12 filed 2026-09-18 after the owner asked whether the design is extensible to backends beyond Rust. Sub-component 3 (cache key ignores the backend) is SPLIT OUT to WI-givib-humiz-pujub-sogip-rosud-bidiz-fupaj-nimal so it can be sequenced: it blocks the backend-agreement measurement (WI-dajif-duzab-notah-guvij-likum-tigir-modoh-rurot), which blocks the config default (WI-hukuf-juniz-zudoh-tivag-kapad-nobuz-komil-rasis). New: producer contract WI-hohuh-jamif-jugim-najak-tufif-goput-lubap-nizok (each backend declares its merge anchor; the merge pass reads it — the key in WI-kokiz-tilam-bohos-tivat-fogil-bijoj-munad-gazid was Rust-shaped and is re-scoped to read the declaration) and recorded-fixture discipline WI-romuh-zakuf-huvug-sokag-rovap-hojol-guzaz-rikup, both blocking WI-kokiz-tilam-bohos-tivat-fogil-bijoj-munad-gazid. Note for the record: ADR-0045 §5's executes_analysed_code declaration is NOT implemented either (grep finds no such field); the contract row lands both declarations on one surface. This row's remaining content is sub-component 4 only (WI-sobig's question); it stays parked."  # e8c2
